# Generated data and outputs. Every pattern here is ANCHORED to the repo root with a
# leading slash. A bare `data/` matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth, which
# silently excluded the source package's own data module
# (src/deeprl_liquidity_provision_uniswapv3/data/: the pool registry, the hourly
# aggregation, the swap-level fee model) from the repository. It was never committed
# and `git status` stayed clean while the code that builds the panel was missing.
/data/**
/outputs/
/old/
/results/
/figs/
/paper/
/RLFin_competition/

# ...but the panel's documentation belongs in the repo, not just on the machine that
# built it. Re-admitting files under an excluded directory needs the directories
# themselves re-admitted first, or git never descends far enough to see them.
!/data/
!/data/**/
!/data/**/*.md
!/data/**/CHECKSUMS.txt


# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#  before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

