*.pyc

# --- before making this repo public again, check ---
# Objects pushed to a repo in a fork network stay reachable by SHA from EVERY other
# repo in that network, including forks that predate the push and never synced.
# Making the parent private does not retract them. So anything committed here should
# be treated as public permanently, whatever the repo's current visibility says.
#
# Keep out: cluster account identifiers (usernames, login hosts, /hpc paths, personal
# email in #SBATCH --mail-user), database credentials, .env files.
# Assistant instructions and internal working notes stay untracked.

# Assistant instruction files and internal working notes stay local and out of the public repository.
/CLAUDE.md
.claude/
/reports/
/SPEC.md
/HANDOVER.md
/DIVERGENCES.md
/AGENTS.md
.codex/

# Generated human-readable reports can contain private machine paths.
/reproducibility/artifacts/**/report.txt
